  "question": {
    "text": "A light ray emits from the origin making an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the positive $x$-axis. After getting reflected by the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, if this ray intersects x-axis at Q, then the abscissa of Q is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZB1ks",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gdlGA",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m9DtB",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bSj4c",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>On plotting the diagram of given data we get,</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/349fee55-7027-45de-9b42-60d31d33691f-9894740.PNG\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 190px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math> reflected by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, the image of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> lies on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></math></p><p>Since it lies on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>On rationalising the numerator we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
